{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852332-i-m-watching-bitten-right-now","id":852332,"title":"I'm Watching Bitten Right Now.....","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-24T04:39:57-07:00","id":852332,"title":"I'm Watching Bitten Right Now.....","content":"Although, I find it hard to watch for more than a few minutes while I sort out stuff or otherwise stress out in my own anxious way. While it's better than <b>Wolf Lake</b>, <b>Being Human</b>, <b>True Blood</b>, <b>Teen Wolf</b>. Has good special effects when they shape shift into Wolves. How they manage themselves (Whatever they call themselves?) and have wolf packs is kind of cool, but this all still seems wrong to me. I still can't get into this. Plus they have all forgone they Crinos shape &amp; only ever use their lesser wolf shape. Yet they're always stronger than normal almost do a inhuman amount of damage just as they are. <br /> <br /> It still lacks a lot of th\u200be charm of earlier movies and werewolf television. Even <b>Buffy the Vampire Slayer's</b> <b>Oz</b> is better than any of this &amp; that's mainly because they don't expect you to take them seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T05:27:58-07:00","id":852345,"title":"","content":"I would advise to read the book; it is actually well thought, well written, and serious.<br /> <br /> Bitten is a MUCH more powerful read than what the TV show offers. As for the Crinos form, well, after all that shape is just a Hollywood invention. In the middle ages all that you got once turned into a werewolf is a wolf body, nothing more. And its clearly said that Bitten's wolf form is superior to normal wolves (your average wolf will have an aproximated weight of 40 kgs, while the supposed B\u00eate du G\u00e9vaudan weighted 60 kgs and it was considered a monstrosity). Bitten wolves all have their human bodyweigth in their animal forms (and transform therefore in really huge wolves, not the size of ponies, but more like a St. Bernard dog), which coupled with their superhuman strenght (which gives them a strenght bonus much like the Crinos form, but being active all time) gives them the capabilities of Urshul more than those of Urhan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T05:49:37-07:00","id":852356,"title":"","content":"I would equate their wolf form closer to Hispo then Lupus in game terms. A lot of players forgo Crinos for Hispo in game if they don't have to use tools. Also like Phersus said, most ancient lore on Werewolves actually has Men becoming Wolves, the half-man/half-wolf hybrid form didn't exist until much later (Even before Hollywood, Like 16-1700's?) when the tales were translated and re-imagined by storytellers looking for a new angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T11:04:54-07:00","id":852494,"title":"","content":"Even though the upright walking hybrid is a thing of <b>Hollywood</b>, I believe my generation have gotten used to that one. It's a kind of done deal with werewolves &amp; especially this game. I seen the book, and think it's for younger people. I'm in my mid forties (Well, just about when I turn 45 at the turn of this year) now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T12:43:14-07:00","id":852543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf-Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852332-i-m-watching-bitten-right-now?p=852494#post852494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even though the upright walking hybrid is a thing of <b>Hollywood</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, as <a href=\"http://www.dailywriting.net/Werewolves_Normandy.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this print of the werewolves of Normandy from the 1800s</a> shows.<br /> <br /> The actual wolf quadrupedal interpretation is the most common, but I've also seen folkloric examples like this and of deranged clearly human figures crawling around on all fours dragging victims with their mouths.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:10:33-07:00","id":852588,"title":"","content":"I once read a book that said that the bipedal wolfman was more common in Eastern European folklore, whereas Western European werewolves tended to be on all fours, with the exception of french werewolves who were also bipedal. Could just be due to different cultural attitudes (either amoung humans or werewolves in-setting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T14:50:05-07:00","id":856731,"title":"","content":"I've seen French werewolves depicted in both ways: the bipedal wolf-headed ones from Normandy, above, and the wolflike quadrupedal ones like the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beast_of_G%C3%A9vaudan\" target=\"_blank\">Beast of G\u00e9vaudan</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}